## Why This Is Asked
Tests CAPA fundamentals under real-world data issues: region awareness, basic data modeling, and a simple remediation flow.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model, lifecycle, REST API, regional metrics, RCA, canary.
- Trade-offs: latency of detection vs noise, data retention for evidence.

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal Express REST endpoints
const express = require('express');
const app = express();
app.use(express.json());
let store = [];
app.post('/caps', (req, res)=>{ const cap={id:Date.now().toString(), ...req.body, status:'detected', created_at:new Date().toISOString()}; store.push(cap); res.status(201).json(cap);});
app.put('/caps/:id', (req,res)=>{ const idx=store.findIndex(c=>c.id===req.params.id); if(idx>=0){store[idx]={...store[idx], ...req.body}; res.json(store[idx]);} else res.status(404).end();});
app.listen(3000);
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate and test the canary plan before broader rollout?
- What telemetry would you capture to ensure no regression after remediation?

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests ability to design a production-grade CAPA for a multi-tenant data platform, emphasizing isolation, auditability, and scalable rollout.

## Key Concepts
- Tenant-scoped CAPA data model with evidence and artifacts
- Immutable links to logs/traces and resource metadata
- Lifecycle state machine and canary-based enforcement
- Per-tenant metrics (recurrence, MTTR, spillover rate)

## Code Example
```javascript
// TypeScript interface for CAPA
interface CAPA {
  id: string;
  tenantId: string;
  policyId: string;
  incidentId: string;
  evidenceLinks: string[];
  artifacts: string[];
  affectedResources: string[];
  dataClassification: string;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle CAPA versioning and backward compatibility?
- How to simulate cross-tenant leakage in a canary without impacting production?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design CAPA from data governance, not just incident response.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model for evidence, artifacts, and policy checks
- Lifecycle state machine with DETECT → INVESTIGATE → CONTAIN → REMEDIATE → VERIFY → CLOSED
- Minimal REST API design for CAPA creation/update with linked traces
- Region-aware compliance metrics (violation rate, MTTR, FP rate)
- RCA template and canary rollout with automated data redaction

## Code Example
```javascript
// CAPA data model sketch (TypeScript)
type CAPARecord = {
  id: string;
  title: string;
  evidenceUrls: string[];
  policyChecks: string[];
  region: string;
  state: 'DETECTED'|'INVESTIGATING'|'CONTAINED'|'REMEDIATED'|'VERIFIED'|'CLOSED';
  createdAt: string;
  updatedAt: string;
};
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you surface policy checks in runtime dashboards?
- How would you automate data redaction in canary tests before broader rollout?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a CAPA program around data governance, cross-region containment, and traceability after a data-leak fault in a deployment.

## Key Concepts
- Data lineage and evidence tagging
- Region-aware CAPA lifecycle gates
- REST API design for CAPA management with linked logs/traces
- Regional leakage metrics and false positive handling
- RCA templates and canary rollback for data sinks

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal CAPA data model in TypeScript
type CAPA = {
  capa_id: string;
  incident_time: string;
  data_class: string;
  evidence_refs: string[];
  lineage: string;
  owner: string;
  remediation: string;
  status: 'IDENTIFY'|'CONTAIN'|'INVESTIGATE'|'REMEDIATE'|'VERIFY'|'CLOSED';
  RCA_id?: string;
}
```

